  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 142 PM EDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\n- Dry through Tuesday, then unsettled\n\nLatest visible loop shows quite a bit of cloudiness moving across\nLower MI in conjunction with a short wave aloft. Once the wave\nmoves east this evening, clearing will occur from the west.\n\nThe large ridge in place over the Great Lakes will get squeezed a\nbit from the large low over the mid Atlantic but won't have much\ninfluence over the cwa this weekend. Instead, we'll see quite a\nbit of sunshine that will carry over into mid week. Highs will\nwarm to the lower to mid 70s by Tuesday before retreating into the\n60s midweek. \n\nThe ridge will break down by Tuesday as a northern stream wave\nmoves across Canada and pushes a cold front across Lower MI. \nConcurrently, a southern stream wave will move east from \nCalifornia across the Southern Rockies. At that point, the \nremnants of Polo will be arriving in New Mexico and get entrained \ninto the southern low. The end result is that that moisture will \nthen ride northeast along the frontal boundary and toward the cwa.\nThe GFS is a bit quicker moving the cold front through compared to\nthe ECMWF, but both models bring rain back into the region as the\nsouthern low moves north. Thus, the latter half of next week looks\nunsettled with periods of showers and isolated thunder.",
